topics.body:
Build each shootout arm's prebuilt Levanter rows from canonical generation traces:
- plain: one clean passing trajectory per eligible task, either the first or the one with the fewest reasoning tokens;
- RS-multi: per epoch, one clean passing attempt per plain task slot, drawn without replacement;
- relay: passing relay episodes with a GLM turn, with each family held to its own share of plain's B;
- recovery: plain's rows, with masked failed attempts and the harness's replies inserted before teacher turns in 20% of rows. A TMax failure is a seeded variant of one of v0's parser-error styles, labeled by the error the vendored Terminus-2 parser gives it;
- validation: one shared set, the first clean passing trajectory per held-out task.

The loss covers GLM's turns only. v0's turns in relay episodes stay as context.

A trajectory is dropped when:
- it was summarized, failed or raised;
- it did not end on the agent's own completion (`--require-clean-completion`: mini-swe-agent's submit, or Terminus-2's `"task_complete": true`);
- it does not fit 32,768 tokens;
- it is listed in `--exclude-trials`, a JSON-lines file of attempts whose pass cannot be trusted (`trial_name`, optional `retry` and `task_id`), applied before selection;
- it leaks: a live proxy capability token (decoded JWT, audience iris-proxy), a read of mini-swe-agent's own tool environment, or a read of a library copy of the task's repo.

Every arm gets the same replay rows: a seeded prefix of the replay slice, cut at R = round(B / 4) and checked by hash against plain's manifest.

Each arm writes three epoch files. Each is its own seeded permutation, padded with zero-loss rows to a multiple of 16, so a trainer that reads files in order with mixture block 16 sees every row exactly once per epoch. The `.gz` files have a fixed gzip header (mtime 0, no file name), so their hashes depend only on their rows.

The manifest records:
- per-epoch row counts, steps and `rows_sha256`;
- per-family supervised and context tokens;
- the builder commit and source hashes;
- `tokenizer_source` (v0 @ 4eeb756b, whose tokenizer files v0.1 shares byte for byte), `parent_model` (v0.1 or v0, via `--parent`) and, on the relay arm, `relay_student`;
- each input trace file's sha256 and Harbor commit, and the excluded trials;
- the token gate over the exact inputs;
- the pool's held-out ids.

A production prefix gets `_SUCCESS` last. `--dry-run` uses the same pins and checks, but writes a `DRY_RUN_NOT_FOR_TRAINING` marker and no `_SUCCESS`.

`chain.py` builds one round's arms from one trace prefix in one command: validation, plain, RS-multi, relay, then recovery, all with the same pool, replay and clean rule. `--relay-trace-prefix` reads relay rounds from a different prefix than plain. Each relay round's `driver_config.json` must name the `--relay-student`. If a relay family ends below plain's B for it, the chain also builds `plain-matched-relay/`, which is plain cut to relay's total in that family, and says so in its summary. `verify_arms.py` then re-reads plain, RS-multi, relay and recovery together, and the matched plain on its own. It checks that no held-out rows are present, that replay rows are shared, that each epoch is a permutation of the same rows, the per-family budgets, and recovery against plain row by row. The chain prints one `CHAIN_BUILT` summary.

A production chain first runs `pool_gate.py` and builds nothing unless it passes. For plain, every shard in the round's shard lists must have `_SUCCESS` and `rebuilt.jsonl`. For relay, each family's `STOP` marker must exist, no round may be uploaded without `_SUCCESS`, and every round with `_SUCCESS` must have its `rebuilt.jsonl`. Every finished shard's traces and requests are then re-scanned for capability tokens, and any hit fails the gate. A running round is invisible to the gate, because a round's directory is uploaded only when it finishes. So all generation jobs must have exited before the build.

`progress.py` and `progress_table.py` report a partial round's arm sizes while generation runs. `reasoning_trim.py` makes dry variants of a built plain arm with long reasoning masked or dropped.

On the round-7 plain traces (GLM at reasoning effort high, pool v5), a dry build at this head gives:
- plain B = 19,418,246 supervised tokens: 7,543,248 SWE-smith and 11,874,998 TMax;
- each epoch is 3,759 rows, or 235 steps at batch 16;
- RS-multi is within 0.76% (SWE) and 1.33% (TMax) of plain's per-family totals;
- recovery injects into 263 of 1,317 SWE rows and 295 of 1,531 TMax rows.

Two builds at the same commit give identical `rows_sha256` and identical `.gz` hashes.

Stacked on #10252, which adds the sweep_data modules this builder imports.

Part of #10213

